WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.978
It was the middle of July, and the hottest day ever.

2
00:00:16.979 --> 00:00:20.626
At least that's how it felt in my room.

3
00:00:20.627 --> 00:00:25.436
My skylight window was open, but it didn't help one bit.

4
00:00:25.437 --> 00:00:32.200
My fan was blowing, but it just seemed to blow more hot air around.

5
00:00:32.201 --> 00:00:36.757
I was even wearing my bathing suit, and I was still hot!

6
00:00:36.758 --> 00:00:40.696
My friends call me "Iggy the Incredible Inventor."

7
00:00:40.697 --> 00:00:44.922
But there was no way I could invent anything today.

8
00:00:44.923 --> 00:00:48.564
It was too hot for me to even think!

9
00:00:48.565 --> 00:00:54.923
Suddenly my fan stopped working.

10
00:00:54.924 --> 00:00:58.900
"Mom!" I called. "It's really hot in here!

11
00:00:58.901 --> 00:01:03.058
Can we get an air conditioner for my room?"

12
00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:06.189
My mom was getting ready to go shopping.

13
00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:12.725
"We can't fit an air conditioner in your tiny room, Iggy," she called from the kitchen.

14
00:01:12.726 --> 00:01:17.320
"Besides, I think the power just went out in the whole building.

15
00:01:17.321 --> 00:01:22.227
The lights aren't working and the air conditioner in the living room turned off."

16
00:01:22.228 --> 00:01:28.820
"My fan isn't working either!" I told her.

17
00:01:28.821 --> 00:01:32.177
My brother, Tate, stuck his head in my room.

18
00:01:32.178 --> 00:01:37.044
"Why don't you stop yelling and invent something?" he said.

19
00:01:37.045 --> 00:01:39.760
"I can't," I said.

20
00:01:39.761 --> 00:01:43.374
"It's so hot in here, my brain won't work."

21
00:01:43.375 --> 00:01:51.269
"Ha-ha!" Tate laughed. "Iggy's brain is melting!"

22
00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:57.912
"That's not funny!" I cried, "Mom! Tate said my brain is melting!"

23
00:01:57.913 --> 00:02:03.597
"I want you two boys to get along while I'm gone," my mother said.

24
00:02:03.598 --> 00:02:10.385
"It's too hot to argue."

25
00:02:10.386 --> 00:02:16.588
A few minutes after my mom left, Molly knocked on our door.

26
00:02:16.589 --> 00:02:20.633
Her little brother, Caswell, was with her.

27
00:02:20.634 --> 00:02:25.716
"Wow," said Molly, sinking down on a chair in our living room.

28
00:02:25.717 --> 00:02:29.602
"It's even hotter in your apartment than it is in ours!

29
00:02:29.603 --> 00:02:35.244
Our power stopped working a few minutes ago."

30
00:02:35.245 --> 00:02:40.602
"The whole building is out of electricity," explained Tate.

31
00:02:40.603 --> 00:02:45.809
"Can you invent something to cool us off, Iggy?" asked Molly.

32
00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:48.951
I shook my head. "Nope."

33
00:02:48.952 --> 00:02:51.513
Caswell was looking at me.

34
00:02:51.514 --> 00:02:56.243
"Why do you have your bathing suit on, Iggy?" he asked.

35
00:02:56.244 --> 00:02:59.412
"Are you going swimming?"

36
00:02:59.413 --> 00:03:03.648
"I was trying to stay cool," I told him.

37
00:03:03.649 --> 00:03:08.064
Just then someone knocked on the door again.

38
00:03:08.065 --> 00:03:11.554
It was Josh and Jenny, from the floor below us.

39
00:03:11.555 --> 00:03:14.810
Josh's dog, Bunch, was with them.

40
00:03:14.811 --> 00:03:18.127
Poor Bunch was hanging his head and panting.

41
00:03:18.128 --> 00:03:23.186
He looked very hot.

42
00:03:23.187 --> 00:03:27.249
I brought him a bowl of water to drink.

43
00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:32.860
"Guess what?" said Jenny, while Bunch lapped noisily from the bowl.

44
00:03:32.861 --> 00:03:36.724
"Our air conditioner blew a fuse."

45
00:03:36.725 --> 00:03:40.730
"What's a fuse?" asked Caswell.

46
00:03:40.731 --> 00:03:44.429
Josh shrugged. "I'm not exactly sure.

47
00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:49.765
But Mr. Calabria said it made all the electricity in the building go out."

48
00:03:49.766 --> 00:03:54.236
"Just like Iggy's brain," said Tate.

49
00:03:54.237 --> 00:03:57.066
"It blew a fuse today too!"

50
00:03:57.067 --> 00:04:01.019
"Very funny," I said, frowning at him.

51
00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:07.079
"Iggy, can you think of a way to stay cool?" asked Jenny.

52
00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:11.543
I was sick of answering this question.

53
00:04:11.544 --> 00:04:14.957
Luckily, Molly answered for me this time.

54
00:04:14.958 --> 00:04:22.166
"Iggy can't think," she said. "He's too hot."

55
00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:27.221
"Wait a minute," I said. "I do have an idea!"

56
00:04:27.222 --> 00:04:30.565
"I hope it's a good one!" said Josh.

57
00:04:30.566 --> 00:04:35.724
"If I get any hotter, I'll blow a fuse too."

58
00:04:35.725 --> 00:04:40.169
"Well, it's not a great idea," I said, grinning.

59
00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:43.960
"But it could lead to a great idea!"

60
00:04:43.961 --> 00:04:47.035
"What is it?" asked Molly.

61
00:04:47.036 --> 00:04:51.077
"I'm going to put an ice pack on my head," I said.

62
00:04:51.078 --> 00:04:53.020
"That will cool off my brain.

63
00:04:53.021 --> 00:05:00.310
Then I'll be able to think of my next incredible invention!"
